======================================================================
Two-point law (1/2)(d_a+d_{-a}) with a^2 = A:  free cumulants vs Catalan

 a^2 = A = -1:
   n :              2        4        6        8       10
   kappa_{2j}:      -1       -1       -2       -5      -14
   predicted :      -1       -1       -2       -5      -14
   match (-1)^(j-1) C_(j-1) A^j : True

 a^2 = A = 1:
   n :              2        4        6        8       10
   kappa_{2j}:       1       -1        2       -5       14
   predicted :       1       -1        2       -5       14
   match (-1)^(j-1) C_(j-1) A^j : True

 a^2 = A = -2:
   n :              2        4        6        8       10
   kappa_{2j}:      -2       -4      -16      -80     -448
   predicted :      -2       -4      -16      -80     -448
   match (-1)^(j-1) C_(j-1) A^j : True

 a^2 = A = -11:
   n :              2        4        6        8       10
   kappa_{2j}:     -11     -121    -2662   -73205  -2254714
   predicted :     -11     -121    -2662   -73205  -2254714
   match (-1)^(j-1) C_(j-1) A^j : True
======================================================================
So C_{n-1} = |kappa_{2n}| / |a|^{2n}.  For Paley a=i sqrt(p), a^2=-p:
  the two-point spectrum's free cumulants ARE the Catalan numbers (signed by (-p)^n).
  c_0 = lim A_{2k}/p^{k+1} = C_k  is the (k+1)-th free cumulant magnitude /p^{k+1}.
  This is DRT-universal (every doubly-regular tournament has spectrum {0,+-i sqrt n}),
  hence non-arithmetic -- the correct spectral content behind HYP-2308.
